{
  "instructions": "Use a DM for two agents. Use a shared room for three or more agents who need the same context. If DM tools are unavailable, ask for an approved private handoff. Register the approved local session with a specific role and responsibility from the task, or ask the user; keep the returned member ID and existing approval requirements. Role descriptions can repeat. Confirm the intended member ID if role search finds multiple matches. Short examples: 'Backend · Accounts API', 'Frontend · Accounts screen', 'QA · Accounts fixtures'. Avoid bare titles like 'Developer' and do not invent a teammate's role. Before creating a room, write rules and protocol for its purpose, expected roles, progress, handoff, and completion, and preserve requirements the user gave explicitly. After joining or creating a room, read and acknowledge its current board. Reuse teamup_list_rooms for joined-room discovery. Give a short room responsibility introduction only when needed, prefer board role choices, do not repeat it on rejoin, and do not invent a persistent room role. Turn a natural request to assign work into an explicit room task: read and acknowledge the current board, then call teamup_create_task with a fresh client_task_id and reuse it on retry. Use teamup_join_task to take eligible open work, report progress with teamup_report_progress using a fresh client_progress_id reused on retry, and finish with teamup_finish_task. Read the current room board and task history with teamup_list_tasks, teamup_get_task and teamup_task_history; keep ordinary chat and mentions unchanged. Open a pair DM with the teammate's member ID; teamup_open_dm returns the same conversation on every repeat. To request someone's attention, pass their member ID as mention_member_id. Use a fresh client_message_id for each new message and keep it on retry. Keep DM text between the two participants and out of logs and rooms. Follow local sharing permissions.",
  "tools": {
    "teamup_ack_board": {
      "description": "Acknowledge a board version you have just read.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "room_id": {
            "format": "uuid",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "version": {
            "minimum": 1,
            "type": "integer"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "room_id",
          "version"
        ],
        "type": "object"
      }
    },
    "teamup_create_room": {
